.PP
\fBtop\fR reads system information exclusively from /proc and from
utmp at /var/run/utmp. On systems where logged-in sessions are tracked
through systemd-logind rather than utmp, the user count in the header
may diverge from what \fBwho\fR(1) or \fBloginctl\fR(1) report.
.PP
Used memory is \fBMemTotal\fR minus \fBMemAvailable\fR. Kernels without
\fBMemAvailable\fR use total minus free, buffers, and reclaimable cache.
The process \fBSHR\fR value is \fBRssFile\fR plus \fBRssShmem\fR in KiB.
.PP
Task summaries count uninterruptible \fBD\fR-state tasks in
\fBd-sleep\fR, separately from the \fBsleep\fR count.
.PP
This is a process-only view: thread mode (\fB\-H\fR) and command-line
sorting (\fB\-o\fR) are not implemented. Interactive P/M/N/T sorting
is available.
